            [r"You forgot $\alpha$: these solve $\cos\theta = \frac{1}{2}$ directly. The equation is $\cos(\theta - 53.1^\circ) = \frac{1}{2}$.", r"You subtracted $\alpha$ from the angles instead of adding it: $\theta - \alpha = 60^\circ$ means $\theta = 60^\circ + 53.1^\circ$.", r"$113.1^\circ$ is right but $53.1^\circ$ is $\alpha$ itself, not a solution: $6\cos 53.1^\circ + 8\sin 53.1^\circ = 10$."],
